 "notes": "DIT SA Standard Road Sign Index sheet (A4, legends and dimensions outlined, colour legend; size from the sheet's size table = register). Every dimension from the sheet; AS 1744 (plus0) spacing. R2-SA51-2A (450 x 900) illustrated (S 300 x 600, B 600 x 1200, C 900 x 1800), 2002, 1:5; R50, white, no outer border. Composite sheet: the sheet dimensions only the assembly and names its parts as AS 1743 signs, so the parts are the national specs — the roundel (R2-6A(R) no right turn, elements copied from tools/specs/R/R2-6 mirrored for the (R) hand.json, its 440 ring at the sheet's 5 margin) and the times panel R9-1-2A (AS 1743 times of operation, two periods, the national spec's layout scaled into the sheet's 442 x 442 box at x 4, y 454: border and edge as panels, letter heights and positions scaled). Vertical chain 5 / 440 (roundel) / 9 / 442 (panel) / 4 = 900; panel 4/442/4 across. Times are the national example (7 - 9 AM, 4.30 - 6.30 PM)."
